  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Crowley Government Services recorded $460M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Crowley Government Services received 255 awards with an average award size of $1.8M, and obligations are down 9.9% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $347M, followed by the Department of Transportation at $110M, the Department of Health and Human Services at $3M, and the Department of Homeland Security at $2.4K. Market concentration skews to transportation and logistics: Deep Sea Freight Transportation accounts for $254M, Freight Transportation Arrangement accounts for $116M, and Ship Building and Repairing accounts for $54.5M. Other Warehousing and Storage accounts for $30.8M, Couriers and Express Delivery Services accounts for $3M, and Petroleum Refineries account for $2.3M. Historical obligations show a peak in FY24 at $728M and a decline to $460M in FY26, after $511M in FY25, $705M in FY23, $429M in FY22, and $426M in FY21. Current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is Crowley Government Services’ current federal footprint?",
        "body": "Crowley Government Services has $460M in obligations in FY2026 to date, spread across 255 awards with an average award size of $1.8M. Crowley Government Services obligations are down 9.9% year over year. Crowley Government Services historical obligations were $426M in FY21, $429M in FY22, $705M in FY23, $728M in FY24, and $511M in FY25."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are Crowley Government Services obligations concentrated by agency and market?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $347M and the Department of Transportation obligated $110M in FY2026 to date. Deep Sea Freight Transportation is the largest market at $254M, followed by Freight Transportation Arrangement at $116M and Ship Building and Repairing at $54.5M. Other Warehousing and Storage accounts for $30.8M, Couriers and Express Delivery Services accounts for $3M, and Petroleum Refineries account for $2.3M."
      }
    ]
